cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  U²-Net-E: Benchmark generalization is not external generalization — a
  controlled study of learned image enhancement for retinal vessel segmentation
message: If you use this code or these results, please cite this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Datta
    given-names: Tapos
repository-code: "https://github.com/tapos-datta/U2NetE_Research"
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of a learnable image-enhancement front-end placed before a
  U²-Net-lite retinal vessel segmenter. The backbone, training recipe and
  evaluation protocol are held fixed and only the input front-end changes.
  Models are trained on 113 images from HRF, CHASE_DB1, DRIVE and STARE and
  evaluated by leave-one-dataset-out testing and once on the external FIVES
  dataset (792 scorable images). The learned front-end gains on the benchmark
  and loses on the external set; diagnostic tests separate a shared
  labelling-convention effect from the module's own deficit, and a multi-scale
  Weber normalization removes that deficit without reliably surpassing no
  enhancement. Every decision stage was preceded by a written pass mark.
keywords:
  - retinal vessel segmentation
  - domain generalization
  - external validation
  - image enhancement
  - leave-one-dataset-out
  - Weber contrast
  - U-Net
  - FIVES
license: Apache-2.0
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
